      "id": 1,
      "text": "Santa Teresa originated around the 1750s Santa Teresa Convent on Desterro hill, becoming Rio's first expansion outside the original Portuguese settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Teresa%2C_Rio_de_Janeiro"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood once housed opulent villas inspired by French architecture, many still standing today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Teresa%2C_Rio_de_Janeiro"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1872 a mule‑drawn tram line connected Santa Teresa to downtown, later electrified in 1896, making it Rio’s first electric tram system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Teresa%2C_Rio_de_Janeiro"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After a 2011 tram accident, the line was modernized and reopened in stages, fully restored to 6 km in 2019.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Teresa%2C_Rio_de_Janeiro"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Parque das Ruínas, a cultural center in Santa Teresa, began as a mansion owned by Laurinda Lobo, a key figure in Rio’s social history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
